<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Resources the shrinker must not remove.

  `isShrinkResources = true` on the release build deletes any resource nothing
  references from code, and everything named here is referenced by nothing:

    - The four licence texts exist to satisfy an obligation. LGPL-2.1 section 6
      says "You must supply a copy of this License" with each copy of the work,
      and the work is the APK. `LicencesScreen` now reads all four through
      `R.raw`, so the shrinker would keep them anyway — but the obligation does
      not depend on a screen continuing to reference them, and losing one to
      resource shrinking would be a licensing regression that no test of the
      debug build could see, because shrinking only runs on release.

    - The two variable fonts are now referenced by `VesselTheme`, so naming them
      here is redundant. Left in place: a theme that stopped referencing a font
      would be a silent fall back to the system family on the release build
      only, and this is the line that stops that being possible.

  Removing a name from this list is a deliberate act. See docs/LICENSING.md.
-->
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:keep="@raw/license_lgpl_2_1,@raw/license_ofl_inter,@raw/license_ofl_jetbrains_mono,@raw/license_bsd_adrenotools,@font/inter_variable,@font/jetbrains_mono_variable" />
